1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,222
What needs attention in your VMware environment?

2
00:00:03,222 --> 00:00:12,888
VMware Skills connects an AI assistant to focused skills and MCP tools, helping engineers investigate infrastructure and plan their next steps.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,638
The family covers vSphere, networking, storage, observability and more.

4
00:00:19,638 --> 00:00:21,818
Pilot coordinates workflows.

5
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:25,727
Domain servers connect to their management systems.

6
00:00:25,727 --> 00:00:30,464
Policy provides shared checks, sanitization and audit logging.

7
00:00:30,464 --> 00:00:33,020
Start with the read-only Monitor.

8
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:38,197
Here is an illustrative example using synthetic data.

9
00:00:38,197 --> 00:00:40,043
Ask what needs attention.

10
00:00:40,043 --> 00:00:44,161
Monitor returns observations about snapshots and storage.

11
00:00:44,161 --> 00:00:50,765
The assistant separates measured facts from missing evidence, then suggests the next checks.

12
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:53,321
No infrastructure changes are made.

13
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:57,178
An old snapshot is an observation.

14
00:00:57,178 --> 00:01:00,557
Future capacity is unknown without trend data.

15
00:01:00,557 --> 00:01:03,577
A report should preserve that difference.

16
00:01:03,577 --> 00:01:12,349
Local configuration, audit logs and exported reports can still write files, even when infrastructure access is read-only.

17
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:19,138
When changes are needed, use the relevant domain skill and a reviewed workflow.

18
00:01:19,138 --> 00:01:23,081
Existing VMware permissions and local policy still apply.

19
00:01:23,081 --> 00:01:26,752
Destructive tools use preview and confirmation gates.

20
00:01:26,752 --> 00:01:32,463
A confirmation flag is not independent human approval, and rollback is best effort.

21
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:38,436
Use the family portal to choose a module and an installation method.

22
00:01:38,436 --> 00:01:41,326
Configure targets and credentials locally.

23
00:01:41,326 --> 00:01:45,895
Begin with a read-only task and validate your model and agent host.

24
00:01:45,895 --> 00:01:49,323
Add other skills only as your workflow needs them.

25
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:56,960
VMware Skills is a community open-source project, not an official VMware or Broadcom product.

26
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:02,919
Explore the demos, try a read-only task, and share what works or what needs improvement.

27
00:02:02,919 --> 00:02:07,605
If it helps your work, star the family portal to help others find it.
